    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="0432" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1594.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Chargé Johnson</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-03T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 3, 1915—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 6, 11 a.m. Department hopes that President’s special message will have
                    favorable results but in the event of failure nothing should be left undone to
                    prevent the enforcement of the old budget or the enactment of any new budget,
                    carrying appropriations in excess of revenue.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
